use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../FilePicker import FilePicker

export ui-component DropZone:
    description:
        A drop zone is an area the user can drag files onto from outside the
        app. It shows when files are being dragged over it and whether they'll
        be accepted, and hands back the files when they're dropped.

    composes:
        - @{FilePicker}

    dragging:
        While files are dragged over it, the zone changes to show it's ready.
        If they won't be accepted, such as the wrong kind of file, it shows
        that instead, before the user lets go. A disabled or read-only zone
        doesn't react to files dragged over it.

    dropping:
        Dropped files are checked against the same limits as a FilePicker:
        which kinds of file, and one or several. The component is told which
        files were accepted, and which were turned away and why.

    missedDrops:
        Files dropped just outside the zone, elsewhere on the page, are ignored
        rather than opened by the platform in place of the app, unless the
        component says otherwise.

    pasting:
        If the component allows it, pasting files while the zone has focus
        adds them as if they had been dropped.

    otherWays:
        Dragging and dropping can't be done from the keyboard, and isn't
        possible for every user. So the zone is also a FilePicker: clicking it,
        or pressing it from the keyboard, opens the file chooser.

    nonGoals:
        - No uploading, progress bars, or previews. It only hands back the files
        - Not for dragging things around inside the app
